Lead client communication, status reporting, planning sessions, and escalations.&nbsp;
Translate model improvement objectives into data requirements, workflows, rubrics, and evaluation plans.&nbsp;
Define quality standards and acceptance criteria for preference data, model comparisons, and evaluation outputs.&nbsp;
Monitor delivery quality, investigate inconsistencies, and resolve ambiguous requirements with clients.&nbsp;
Advise on data design, evaluation approaches, and project feasibility based on your domain expertise.&nbsp;
Develop reusable guidelines, SOPs, and QA frameworks to improve consistency across programs.&nbsp;
Mentor Operations Specialists and contribute to project scoping, pilots, and new capability development.&nbsp;
What You Bring
1–2+ years of experience in AI data operations, project coordination, or delivery, ideally in a GenAI or frontier AI environment.
Familiarity with at least one AI post-training or model evaluation workflow.&nbsp;
Experience coordinating projects or workstreams, managing stakeholders, and communicating with clients.
Understanding of data quality, annotation workflows, and quality assurance methods.
Ability to translate evolving requirements into clear workflows, rubrics, and measurable quality standards.&nbsp;
Strong troubleshooting and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities.&nbsp;
Interest in current AI developments, including frontier models and post-training approaches.&nbsp;
Nice to Have
Experience with reinforcement learning from human feedback (RLHF), preference data, or model response evaluation.
Familiarity&nbsp;with rubric design, model comparison, benchmark development, or evaluation creation.
Experience assessing model responses for quality, accuracy, reasoning, or instruction following.
Exposure to AI companies, frontier AI labs, or model evaluation programs.
Bilingual capabilities, particularly German or a Nordic language.&nbsp;
Why You'll Love Working Here
At Appen, we foster a culture of innovation, collaboration, and excellence. We value curiosity, accountability, and a commitment to delivering the highest quality AI solutions for frontier models.
You'll work on complex challenges that shape the future of AI across industries and geographies, alongside talented people in a culture that values humility over ego. You'll have the flexibility to deliver in a way that works for you and your team, supported by tools, resources, and development opportunities to continue to build your capability over time.
