Caseware is one of Canada's original Fintech companies, having led the global audit and accounting software industry for over 30 years, with more than 500,000 users across 130 countries and available in 16 different languages. While you might not have heard of us (yet) over 36,000 accounting and audit professionals list Caseware as a skill on their LinkedIn profiles!As Product Owner for our Cloud solutions, you are responsible for driving the development, maintenance, and continuous improvement of our products. You work closely with a full team—both functional and development—so affinity with both is important. You organize and prioritize the team’s work through a well-managed backlog and sprint board, ensuring delivery of maximum value to our customers.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
❗This is a Full time permanent position
&nbsp;
📍&nbsp;Location:&nbsp;&nbsp;
This is a&nbsp;hybrid&nbsp;role requiring the successful candidate to work&nbsp; 3&nbsp;days a week in our Apeldoorn, Netherlands office, located at Fauststraat 3, 7323 BA Apeldoorn, NetherlandsWhat you will be doing:
Drive the development, maintenance, and continuous improvement of our Cloud products.
Collaborate closely with a full team—both functional and development—so affinity with both is important.
Organize and prioritize the team’s work through a well-managed backlog and sprint board.
Ensure delivery of maximum value to our customers.
Define the product roadmap in alignment with strategic goals and market developments.
Coach the team to stay aligned with our overall product vision.
Focus on financial reporting, audit, and related workflows for the Dutch accountancy market.
Act as the final responsible for the success of our Cloud solutions.
Understand customer needs and balance various stakeholder demands.
Translate insights into clear product decisions and priorities.
Share progress regularly via roadmap presentations and other communications.
Create clarity and alignment across internal and external stakeholders.
What you will bring:
Experience or a strong affinity with audit and accounting (hands-on experience in practice is a plus)
Possesses deep understanding of the Dutch market and user needs
Supports the team in delivering accurate, high-quality, and compliant product content
Works effectively both independently and collaboratively, with excellent prioritization skills
Excels at translating complex concepts into intuitive, user-friendly solutions
Is available full-time and ready to take ownership as a proactive leader within the team
What's in it for you:
&nbsp;
▪️Innovation is at our core. We work with cutting-edge technology in accounting and financial reporting, constantly pushing the boundaries to create impactful software solutions.&nbsp;
▪️We are committed to a collaborative culture, where your ideas are valued, and knowledge sharing is encouraged within a supportive, inclusive team.&nbsp;
▪️Work-life balance is important to us. We offer flexible work options, remote opportunities, and generous time-off policies to ensure a healthy work-life balance.&nbsp;
▪️We offer competitive compensation, including a competitive salary and comprehensive benefits
▪️We are driven by impactful work. Your contributions directly affect how our clients manage financial processes and drive their success.&nbsp;
▪️Recognition and rewards matter to us. We celebrate hard work through recognition programs, performance bonuses, and opportunities for career growth.&nbsp;
▪️We embrace global opportunities. Work on international projects and collaborate with a diverse, global team.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
About Caseware:
Caseware's cutting-edge software products are meticulously designed for accounting firms, corporations, and governments.&nbsp;Our teams are continually collaborating, innovating, and building upon our existing suite of products. With a customer-focused mindset, we are building technology that is shaping what the future of audits, financial reporting, and financial data analytics will look like.
&nbsp;
With a recent strategic investment from Hg Capital in 2020, Caseware is now in its next major growth phase as we double down on the people and products that have made Caseware so successful to date.
&nbsp;
One of Caseware's core values is Many Voices, One Team and with that in mind, we're dedicated to building teams as diverse as our customers in an equitable and inclusive way. We welcome and encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply. Should you require accommodations or have any questions at any point during the application or interview process, please e-mail our People Operations team at -----
