&lt;div class=&quot;description content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.thoughtworks.com/&quot;&gt;Thoughtworks&lt;/a&gt; is a global technology consultancy that integrates design, engineering and AI to drive digital innovation. We are over 10,000 people strong across 47 offices in 18 countries. For 30+ years, we’ve delivered extraordinary impact together with our clients by helping them solve complex business problems with technology and culture as the differentiator.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Thoughtworks.com is one of our most important customer-facing products, helping clients discover our expertise, explore evidence of our impact and take the next step with us. It also helps job seekers explore opportunities and gives search engines and AI assistants an accurate, trusted understanding of who we are and what we do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, fragmented ownership across Marketing limits our ability to deliver connected customer journeys, maintain consistent quality and continuously improve performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Head of Product Design to change that. You’ll lead Thoughtworks.com as a digital product, translating our go-to-market and employer brand strategies into seamless experiences for customers, job seekers and AI agents. You’ll own the website strategy, roadmap, customer journeys, publishing model and content and design quality. You&#39;ll also shape experiences across connected channels, including email through Knak and events through Splash, while influencing the internal workflows that drive quality, consistency and speed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, player-coach role for someone who can think strategically and deliver at every level, from defining roadmaps and improving customer journeys to refining copy, reviewing designs, interpreting performance data and making launch decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;job-responsibilities&quot;&gt;Job responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-responsibilities content&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Website product strategy&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the product vision, principles and roadmap for Thoughtworks.com&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize work around customer and business outcomes rather than requests for individual pages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect the website roadmap to Thoughtworks’ go-to-market priorities, propositions and major company launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer journeys and experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a deep understanding of our audiences, including enterprise buyers, technology leaders, practitioners, partners, prospective employees and alumni community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design connected journeys that help people move from a question/problem/need to relevant services, expertise, evidence and action, where the site fuels journeys on AI platforms that might never have users interact with our site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use customer research, website data and market insight to identify friction and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the core website, event pages and email experiences work together where they form part of the same journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Narrative, copy and content quality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the quality and coherence of the website narrative, copy and information architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex technology services and Thoughtworks expertise into clear, credible experiences for different audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge unclear propositions, duplicated content, unsupported claims and pages that do not serve a defined customer need&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the central Content team, service-line marketers and subject-matter experts, while keeping accountability for how content works within the overall experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with content operations to establish reusable content patterns, editorial standards and clear ownership for maintaining important content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experiences for people and agents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the website is useful and understandable to human visitors, search engines and AI assistants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the SEO and LLM Discoverability Lead to improve how Thoughtworks is found, interpreted and represented to support buyers in their decision making process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape requirements for structured content, metadata, evidence, content relationships and reusable information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance machine readability with strong human storytelling, accessibility and brand expression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Publishing model for the AI era&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the spec for redesigning the publishing workflow from brief through design, production, approval, release and ongoing improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the GTM tech and Global IT teams to replace manual, error-prone production with reusable patterns, clearer decision rights and proportionate automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify where AI can improve research, prototyping, content preparation, metadata, accessibility checks, quality assurance and content maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn good judgment into practical standards, templates, playbooks and automated checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a model that allows teams to move faster without lowering the quality bar or creating uncontrolled publishing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design quality and experimentation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the direction and quality bar for UX, UI, interaction design and the website design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use qualitative and quantitative evidence to improve journeys, messaging and conversion over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sign off on experience quality before major launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team and agency leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a multidisciplinary team spanning product design, experience production, transformation and discoverability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give people clear outcomes, decision rights, constructive feedback and room to do excellent work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an effective working model with the central Content team, GTM technology, Global IT and service-line marketers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;job-qualifications&quot;&gt;Job qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-qualifications content&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;technical-skills&quot;&gt;Technical Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;qualifications inner-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 - 15 years experience leading digital products, customer experiences, service design or product design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong record of turning customer insight and business strategy into coherent end-to-end experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent judgment across product, UX, content and design, with the ability to recognize and explain what good looks like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong writing and editorial instincts, including the confidence to simplify complex ideas and challenge unclear copy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with marketing, product, design, engineering and senior business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial understanding and the ability to connect digital experience decisions to go-to-market outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems thinking, including experience creating reusable patterns, design systems, operating models or publishing frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of search, structured content and how AI assistants discover and interpret information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI tools to improve how work is researched, designed, produced or assured&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to operate in ambiguity, make difficult prioritization decisions and move from strategy to delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of leading and coaching people or multidisciplinary teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;professional-skills&quot;&gt;Professional Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;skills inner-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a natural ability to establish and nurture relationships with senior leaders across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have excellent context-switching capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in situations where you are given little to no direction and have the ability to lead, organize and deliver commitments on time and within budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re resilient in ambiguous situations and can adapt your role to approach challenges from multiple perspectives. You don’t shy away from risks, instead you take them on and skillfully manage them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re empathetic and use this ability to build solid working relationships and resolve issues quickly and thoughtfully&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;important-things&quot;&gt;Other things to know&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;important-things content&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;inner-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is no one-size-fits-all career path at Thoughtworks: however you want to develop your career is entirely up to you. But we also balance autonomy with the strength of our cultivation culture. This means your career is supported by interactive tools, numerous development programs and teammates who want to help you grow. We see value in helping each other be our best and that extends to empowering our employees in their career journeys.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;responsible-ai-use&quot;&gt;Responsible Use of AI in Recruitment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;responsible-ai-use content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Thoughtworks, we use AI tools to support our recruitment team with administrative tasks such as drafting communications, scheduling interviews and writing job descriptions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Crucially, our AI tools do not screen, assess, rank or make hiring decisions. Every application is reviewed by our team and all selection decisions are made exclusively by our interviewers and hiring managers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to fairness and responsible AI. We actively manage our AI systems by testing, monitoring for biased outcomes and implementing mitigation measures. We hold our third-party vendors to these same high standards through a rigorous governance process. For additional information, please see our full &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.thoughtworks.com/careers/ai-policy-for-recruitment&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Thoughtworks AI Policy for Recruitment&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about&quot;&gt;About Thoughtworks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;about content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thoughtworks is a dynamic and inclusive community of bright and supportive colleagues who are revolutionizing tech. As a leading technology consultancy, we’re pushing boundaries through our purposeful and impactful work. For 30+ years, we’ve delivered extraordinary impact together with our clients by helping them solve complex business problems with technology as the differentiator. Bring your brilliant expertise and commitment for continuous learning to Thoughtworks. Together, let’s be extraordinary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;display: none;&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.thoughtworks.com/careers/ai-policy-for-recruitment&quot;&gt;See here our AI policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Explore how a next-generation AI architecture behaves from rack scale to data centre scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Systems Engineer, you will investigate a novel AI computing architecture under demanding real-world workloads. You will work on problems where answers aren&#39;t readily known, turning curiosity into measurable evidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will design experiments, benchmark representative AI workloads and explore how hardware components and software interact at scale. When behaviour is unexpected, you will turn this into new measurements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your work will help infrastructure engineers, architects and application specialists understand system behaviour, performance, scalability and reliability across the stack. You will also help develop tooling and automation to collect, analyse and visualise system metrics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You do not need to be an AI expert. You will need strong judgement, curiosity and a clear preference for evidence over opinion. You will love this role if you are someone who takes initiative, questions assumptions and enjoys working in areas where the answers are not yet known.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team and culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The System QA team is distributed across multiple locations. We work hard to stay connected and collaborate closely. Our daily team meetings feel more like a virtual coffee break than a formal status update with space to share ideas, ask questions, discuss discoveries and solve problems together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value trust, autonomy and openness, and we understand that great engineers don&#39;t all follow the same career path. What matters is the quality of your work, your curiosity, and your willingness to explore challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have regular 1:1s with your people manager where you will have the opportunity to discuss things that matter to you. You will have dedicated time each week to focus on your CPD. The technical lead will provide direction and help set priorities, but everyone in the team is there to support each other.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One of our core principles is that we measure and report what we observe without trying to make results look better or worse than they are.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using Python to write tests, automate tasks, analyse data or develop practical engineering tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A curiosity-driven approach to investigating complex systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to explain technical findings clearly, using accurate and reproducible evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence to work independently, take responsibility and collaborate across engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in some of the following would be valuable: AI workloads and benchmarking, systems architecture, parallel and distributed computing, automation, containers or modern orchestration infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences from different industries. We actively welcome applications from engineers to the profession through a returnship or after a career break.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working: Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous leave: Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement planning support: Up to 5% matched pension&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Phantom equity: Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workplace experience: Enjoy thoughtfully designed office spaces for collaboration, with free food and an on-site barista to support your day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Peace of mind protection: Income protection and life assurance to provide financial security for you and your loved ones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible benefits: Tailor your benefits package with a choice of additional options, including private medical insurance and dental cover&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optional benefits: Dental cover, health cash plan, private medical insurance, cycle to work scheme, give as you earn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know - we’re happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sponsorship&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the UK. Unfortunately, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support visa applications for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join the Team at Graphcore&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore is one of the world’s leading innovators in Artificial Intelligence compute. It is developing hardware, software and systems infrastructure that will unlock the next generation of AI breakthroughs and power the widespread adoption of AI solutions across every industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. Together, they share a bold vision: to enable Artificial Super Intelligence and ensure its benefits are accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore’s teams are drawn from diverse backgrounds and bring a broad range of skills and perspectives. A melting pot of AI research specialists, silicon designers, software engineers and systems architects, Graphcore brings together deep expertise to solve complex problems and deliver meaningful progress in AI compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to explore how complex AI systems really behave, we’d love to hear from you. Apply now to join the Systems Engineering team.&lt;/p&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;h3&gt;About the job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the system software organisation that turns complex hardware platforms into reliable Graphcore systems.&amp;nbsp;As Director of System Software, you will report to the VP of Software and turn software strategy into clear priorities, plans and outcomes. You will lead the teams delivering firmware, drivers, OpenBMC and system software QA.&amp;nbsp;Your work will shape platform bring-up, production release and long-term support across Graphcore systems. You will align technical decisions with business priorities, delivery milestones and product readiness.&amp;nbsp;You will build a strong engineering organisation, developing managers, technical leaders and engineers. You will own execution, quality and cross-functional delivery across hardware, silicon, software and product teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for a leader who can think big, act fast and take responsibility for complex system outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The team and culture&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;System Software works close to the hardware, where small decisions can shape product reliability at scale. The team operates through clear ownership, evidence-based planning and direct technical debate.&amp;nbsp;You will lead managers and specialists across firmware, drivers, OpenBMC and QA. Decisions are made through engineering judgement, clear trade-offs and a strong focus on delivery impact.&amp;nbsp;You will be expected to speak up, challenge assumptions and help resolve issues across hardware and software boundaries. Pace matters, but so do maintainability, security and long term quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· A strong track record leading system software teams across closely coupled hardware and software programmes.&lt;br&gt;· Experience managing managers or multiple technical teams, with clear ownership of delivery outcomes.&lt;br&gt;· Proven ability to build, coach and develop engineering leaders through change and technical uncertainty.&lt;br&gt;· Strong judgement across planning, resourcing, dependencies, risk and production release readiness.&lt;br&gt;· Experience embedding validation, automated testing, hardware-in-the-loop testing and clear release criteria.&lt;br&gt;· Credible technical breadth across firmware, drivers, OpenBMC, QA or related low-level software domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. We also welcome engineers returning to the profession after a career break, including through returnship routes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Flexible working: Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;br&gt;· Generous leave: Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;· Retirement planning support: Up to 5% matched pension&lt;br&gt;· Phantom equity: Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;br&gt;· Workplace experience: Enjoy thoughtfully designed office spaces for collaboration, with free food and an on-site barista to support your day&lt;br&gt;· Peace of mind protection: Income protection and life assurance to provide financial security for you and your loved ones&lt;br&gt;· Electric Vehicle Scheme: Choose an electric vehicle and lease it through salary sacrifice&lt;br&gt;· Flexible benefits: Tailor your benefits package with a choice of additional options, including private medical insurance and dental cover&lt;br&gt;· Optional benefits: Dental cover, health cash plan, private medical insurance, cycle to work scheme, give as you earn&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;br&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know - we’re happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Join the Team at Graphcore&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore is one of the world’s leading innovators in Artificial Intelligence compute. It is developing hardware, software and systems infrastructure that will unlock the next generation of AI breakthroughs and power the widespread adoption of AI solutions across every industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. Together, they share a bold vision: to enable Artificial Super Intelligence and ensure its benefits are accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore’s teams are drawn from diverse backgrounds and bring a broad range of skills and perspectives. A melting pot of AI research specialists, silicon designers, software engineers and systems architects, Graphcore brings together deep expertise to solve complex problems and deliver meaningful progress in AI compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to lead the system software organisation behind Graphcore’s next generation platforms, we’d love to hear from you. Apply now to be part of the journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Sponsorship&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the UK. Unfortunately, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support visa applications for this role.&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;500M+ downloads. 80M+ monthly users. A decade of building – and we’re still accelerating.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flo is the world’s #1 health &amp;amp; fitness app worldwide on a mission to build a better future for female health. Backed by a $200M investment led by General Atlantic, we became the first product of our kind to reach a $1B valuation in 2024 – and we’re not slowing down.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With 7M paid subscribers and the highest-rated experience in the App Store’s health category, we’ve spent 10 years earning trust at scale. Now, we’re building the next generation of digital health – AI-powered, privacy-first, clinically backed – to help our users know their body better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Infrastructure Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than 80 million women open Flo every month to understand their bodies and their health. Every one of those sessions runs on infrastructure we build, and the data behind it is as personal as data gets. Keeping that fast and private at this scale is the job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Velocity runs the platform that every Flo engineer builds on: Kubernetes on AWS, the data stores behind our services, and the golden paths that let product teams ship without needing to be infrastructure experts. We treat our internal developers as our customers. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the foundations:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and run the Kubernetes and data infrastructure behind 80 million monthly active users, and make it boring in the best sense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn expertise into self-service:&lt;/strong&gt; Take what you know about running clusters and databases well, and build it into the defaults so product teams get it for free.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes at scale:&lt;/strong&gt; Architect and evolve our EKS estate: cluster lifecycle and upgrades, networking, autoscaling, workload isolation, and the Helm and Terraform that deploy onto it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data infrastructure:&lt;/strong&gt; Shape how our services use PostgreSQL, DynamoDB and Kafka. Set the patterns for provisioning, access, backup, failover and capacity, so teams aren&#39;t solving these problems one service at a time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Golden paths:&lt;/strong&gt; Build self-service tooling and Terraform modules that give product teams autonomy without sacrificing stability or security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reliability:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead resilience work, including business continuity planning, disaster recovery testing and a sustainable on-call rotation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy at scale:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the infrastructure behind privacy features such as our TIME-recognised &quot;Anonymous Mode&quot;, and keep us SOC2, ISO 27001 and ISO 27701 certified while handling some of the most sensitive data there is.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability:&lt;/strong&gt; Make sure metrics, logs and traces tell us something is wrong before our users do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Many years in infrastructure, platform, SRE or DevOps roles running high-traffic, distributed systems in production. You have operated at Principal or Staff scope, setting direction across teams as well as delivering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes depth:&lt;/strong&gt; You have run Kubernetes in production for real workloads, ideally EKS. You can explain what happens between kubectl apply and a pod serving traffic, and you have debugged it when it didn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data infrastructure awareness:&lt;/strong&gt; You understand how PostgreSQL, DynamoDB and Kafka behave under load and when they fail: connection limits, replication lag, hot partitions, consumer lag, retention. You don&#39;t need to have been a DBA, but you know what good looks like and when to ask for help.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AWS and infrastructure as code:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong AWS knowledge and fluent Terraform. Coding experience in Go or Python is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; A doc-first habit, and the ability to bring distributed product teams with you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI first: you will have seen the impact AI automation is having on development teams and the software delivery lifecycle, and have strong ideas on how infrastructure should support it.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hardening infrastructure for high-compliance or security-sensitive environments (HIPAA, SOC 2, PCI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running managed data services in AWS (RDS, Aurora, MSK, DynamoDB) at scale, including migrations and major version upgrades.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaling consumer platforms with millions of concurrent users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certifications such as AWS Certified Solutions Architect Professional, CKA or CKS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Flo?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High impact:&lt;/strong&gt; Flo is used by 1 in 4 women aged 18–44 in the US, and has raised $200M to build what comes next.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; We hire experts and trust them to deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modern stack at scale:&lt;/strong&gt; EKS, Terraform, Kafka, PostgreSQL, DynamoDB and Sentry, serving more than 80 million people a month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary Range (ranges may vary based on skills and experience)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£130,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£150,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a mission-led, product-driven team. We move fast, stay focused and take ownership – from brief to build to impact. Debate is encouraged. Decisions are shared. We care about craft, ship with purpose, and always raise the bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be working with people who take their work seriously, not themselves. It takes commitment, resilience, and the drive to keep going when things get tough. Because better health outcomes are worth it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll get&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support impact with meaningful reward. Here’s what that looks like:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and annual reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to participate in Flo’s performance incentive scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid holiday, sick leave, and female health leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced parental leave and pay for maternity, paternity, same-sex and adoptive parents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerated professional growth through world-changing work and learning support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-person collaboration and work in a hybrid model, with 3 days per week spent in the office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-week fully paid sabbatical at 5-year Floversary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flo Premium for friends &amp;amp; family, plus more health, pension and wellbeing perks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, equity and inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our strength is in our differences. At Flo, hiring is based on merit, skill and what you bring to the role – nothing else. We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds, communities and identities. Read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://flo.health/privacy-policy-for-job-applicants&quot;&gt;privacy notice for job applicants&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UX Researcher&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: Bristol/London, UK (hybrid, three days a week in the office)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team: UX&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary: £58,000 - £70,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contract: Permanent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reporting To: UX Lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note: This role requires an existing right to work in the UK. We can’t offer visa sponsorship, but we review sponsorship role by role, so keep an eye on our careers site for future opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About Kaluza&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kaluza is the Energy Intelligence Platform, turning energy complexity into seamless coordination. We help energy companies overcome today’s challenges while accelerating the shift to a clean, electrified future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our platform orchestrates millions of real-time decisions across homes, devices, markets and grids. By combining predictive algorithms with human-centred design, Kaluza makes clean energy dependable, affordable and adaptive to everyday life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With teams across Europe, Asia and Australia, and a joint venture with Mitsubishi Corporation in Japan, we power leading companies including OVO, AGL and ENGIE, as well as innovators like Volvo and Volkswagen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on research&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run mixed-methods research in a B2B2C setting, combining qualitative studies with behavioural data in Mixpanel, that sets the standard for good research and shapes team roadmaps and client conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research the whole chain, from client teams and subject matter experts to their end customers and the developers using our SDKs and APIs, and look for patterns that hold across clients so we build once and reuse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure research has impact: track whether it changed a decision and what result followed, and use that to make the case for research investment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Research enablement and operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Democratise research: coach and mentor colleagues in Product, Design and Engineering to run their own studies with rigour, through workshops, guidance and lightweight methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make insight easy to find and trust, through our insights agents, knowledge bases and journey management artefacts, backed by data you can rely on (quality, privacy, bias), so people can find and question evidence themselves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help run research operations: improve how we recruit participants (frameworks, lead times, consent and data protection), and set clear guardrails so teams run ethical, compliant research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess and recommend research tools, deciding when to build and when to buy, trial them, and support procurement; use AI-assisted development such as Claude Code to build working tools where that is the right call&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring &lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ideally you’ll have/be&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of running research end to end that other teams used in product or roadmap decisions, with strong data literacy: you combine qualitative methods with behavioural data and know what the numbers can and can’t tell us&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience researching in B2B or B2B2C or enterprise contexts, including technical users such as developers (eg SDKs, APIs or documentation), or a strong appetite to learn how&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coaching non-researchers in research fundamentals (interviewing, bias mitigation, ethical handling of user data) so they can self-serve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience on a platform or multi-client product, spotting patterns across customers, and familiarity with journey mapping or service design methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in research operations or enablement, such as participant recruitment, consent and data governance, repositories or tool selection, with judgement on when to build and when to buy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence working with some autonomy across a distributed, international team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will set you apart&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve built a tool, repository or pipeline that measurably cut the time from research signal to team-wide insight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve found a way to measure developer experience where there was no playbook (eg time to first successful call, or where developers drop off)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve made the case for research with real numbers, and followed your research after the readout to see what happened&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you&#39;ll work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We offer flexible working, with an expectation of 3 days a week in the office. This gives us the best of both: real time together to collaborate and build relationships, with the flexibility to work in the way that suits you best the rest of the week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Play to win:&lt;/strong&gt; Collective pride in decarbonising energy at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solve the real problem:&lt;/strong&gt; Cutting through complexity to focus on real-world outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build trust every day:&lt;/strong&gt; Consistency, transparency and doing what we say.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the outcome:&lt;/strong&gt; Full accountability, wins and setbacks, without ego.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go further together: &lt;/strong&gt;Collaboration, respect and different perspectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time off and family:&lt;/strong&gt; 26 days’ holiday, plus 26 weeks’ full pay for new parents with no qualifying service period&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health and security:&lt;/strong&gt; Private medical insurance with virtual GP, life assurance, pension scheme, free mortgage advice and eye tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay and flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Discretionary bonus, a Flex Fund of 5% [of salary] to spend on the benefits you want most, retail discounts through Perks at Work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth and setup:&lt;/strong&gt; Personal learning budget, home office budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Climate:&lt;/strong&gt; Furthr, our climate action app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come as you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want to meet people from all walks of life. The more inclusive we are, the better our work will be, and we recognise talent on merit and potential. If you’re excited about the role but don’t tick every box, we’d still love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find out more on our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kaluza.com/careers/&quot;&gt; careers page&lt;/a&gt; and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/kaluza/&quot;&gt; LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;. Our Applicant Data Protection Policy is&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kaluza.com/applicant-data-protection-notice/&quot;&gt; here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;job__header&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job__title&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 class=&quot;section-header section-header--large font-primary&quot;&gt;Software Engineer III - Data - FMX&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job__location&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;United Kingdom&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job__description body&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;message-list_1784585771.303139&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Data Engineer III&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Data Engineer III to join our Data Engineering team, which builds and governs the data foundation that powers the business. You&#39;ll work within our stack — Python ingestion pipelines, Airflow orchestration, and Snowflake/Databricks — helping move data reliably and securely from source to decision-ready output.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll implement features and fixes against a given design, handle known classes of pipeline issues on your own, and escalate genuinely novel problems with clear context rather than working them in isolation. You&#39;re also expected to start contributing meaningfully in code review — catching real bugs, not just style nits.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement new ingestion sources end-to-end against a senior engineer&#39;s design — connector code, DAG, schema, monitoring, and catalog registration — extending the team&#39;s existing framework where a new source needs a pattern it doesn&#39;t yet support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate pipeline failures independently, recognize known classes of issues, and ship the documented fix without needing to escalate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Before shipping a new pipeline, identify downstream consumers and what would break if data were late or wrong, and flag gaps like this during spec review — before writing code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear handovers when escalating a genuinely unresolved issue — what you tried, what you ruled out, and where things diverge — so a senior can pick up without re-discovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review peers&#39; pipeline PRs and catch non-obvious issues (e.g., missing idempotency checks, race conditions) that could cause incorrect downstream data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn ambiguous &quot;why is this data wrong?&quot; questions into structured investigations — tracing data lineage from source to warehouse and communicating back what you found&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface concerns in spec review as specific, well-reasoned questions rather than staying silent or blocking progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support data security and governance work (e.g., PII masking, access controls) and contribute to data delivery work, including reverse ETL integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong working relationships with internal stakeholders and help scope and clarify requirements for new work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor DE2s on their first significant projects — pairing on tricky decisions and helping them apply team conventions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of professional software or data engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL and Python skills, with solid experience building and operating production data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort investigating and root-causing pipeline issues independently before escalating&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with workflow orchestration tools (Airflow or similar) and a cloud data warehouse/lakehouse (Snowflake, Databricks, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of data pipeline concepts: idempotency, schema evolution, backfills, and data quality/testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience giving substantive code review feedback, not just style or formatting comments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills — can write a clear technical handover, ask sharp questions in spec review, and explain a data lineage investigation to a non-technical stakeholder&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of taking ownership of known-class problems end-to-end rather than needing step-by-step direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience extending or building reusable pipeline frameworks/templates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to reverse ETL tools or patterns, PII masking, or data access governance (RBAC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to observability/monitoring tooling (e.g., Datadog) for pipeline health and alerting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some experience mentoring or informally supporting more junior engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in gaming, betting, e-commerce, or another regulated/high-compliance industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real ownership over known-class problems, with senior/staff support available for the genuinely novel ones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on high-visibility, high-trust systems that the business depends on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A culture built around clear tenets: standardize before you scale, own the outcome (not just the ticket), and clarity over complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear growth path into Senior Data Engineer, with room to start mentoring and shaping team practices along the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a -----
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Are you someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment, where you are given the autonomy and support to handle large amounts of responsibility?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Are you looking for the opportunity to accelerate your sales career whilst also being surrounded by an exceptional entrepreneurial team with motivated and extremely driven people?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be responsible for managing and growing a portfolio of sponsors across our international conferences, building long-term relationships with senior decision-makers and driving sponsorship revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-performance B2B sales role with a strong focus on sponsor retention, renewals and account growth, alongside identifying and closing new sponsorship opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a commercially driven salesperson who enjoys building strong client relationships, growing accounts and consistently delivering against revenue targets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At least 2 years of B2B sales experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A proven track record of achieving or exceeding individual revenue targets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience managing client relationships, retaining customers and identifying opportunities to grow existing accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Confidence engaging, pitching and negotiating with senior decision-makers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong commercial instincts and the ability to identify new revenue opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ambition, resilience and ownership – you take responsibility for your portfolio, performance and results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent communication and relationship-building skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;This role might not be the right fit if...&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You prefer a role focused purely on relationship management, without responsibility for sales and revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t enjoy negotiating, closing deals and working towards commercial targets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re not comfortable taking ownership of client relationships and proactively identifying opportunities to grow accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re looking for a hybrid or remote position – our London team works together from the office five days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage and retain sponsors:&lt;/strong&gt; Build strong, long-term relationships with an existing portfolio of sponsors, driving renewals and repeat business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow existing accounts:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify opportunities to upsell, cross-sell and increase sponsorship revenue within your portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive new business:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify, pitch and close new sponsorship opportunities to expand our client base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own your revenue targets:&lt;/strong&gt; Take responsibility for achieving ambitious individual sales and retention targets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver exceptional partnerships:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with our content and delivery teams to ensure sponsors receive a high-quality experience and see value in their partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What we offer&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Competitive salary and market-leading OTE.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Significant ownership and responsibility from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The opportunity to work closely with our senior leadership team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;International travel to our conferences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Training, coaching and ongoing development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong opportunities for internal progression as we continue to grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CFO Insights is a leading Northern European community for CFOs, finance executives and future finance leaders. Through our conferences and events, we bring together senior finance professionals to exchange insights, explore the evolving role of finance and build valuable business relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CFO Insights is part of United Media, a global B2B media and conferences group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start date:&lt;/strong&gt; As soon as possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Monday–Friday, we work from our &lt;strong&gt;WeWork office in Victoria, London&lt;/strong&gt;. Due to the collaborative nature of our work, we do not offer remote work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You must have the &lt;strong&gt;right to work in the UK&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Level Up Your Career with Zynga!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Zynga, we bring people together through the power of play. As a global leader in interactive entertainment and a proud label of Take-Two Interactive, our games have been downloaded over 6 billion times—connecting players in 175+ countries through fun, strategy, and a little friendly competition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From thrilling casino spins to epic strategy battles, mind-bending puzzles, and social word challenges, our diverse game portfolio has something for everyone. Fan-favorites and latest hits include FarmVille™, Words With Friends™, Zynga Poker™, Game of Thrones Slots Casino™, Wizard of Oz Slots™, Hit it Rich! Slots™, Wonka Slots™, Top Eleven™, Toon Blast™, Empires &amp;amp; Puzzles™, Merge Dragons!™, CSR Racing™, Harry Potter: Puzzles &amp;amp; Spells™, Match Factory™, and Color Block Jam™—plus many more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2007 and headquartered in California, our teams span North America, Europe, and Asia, working together to craft unforgettable gaming experiences. Whether you&#39;re spinning, strategizing, matching, or competing, Zynga is where fun meets innovation—and where you can take your career to the next level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and be part of the play!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At NaturalMotion, we make games that wow people. We innovate to create previously impossible experiences that would not exist without us. We take pride in making titles that reach a large audience and creating communities that last. Our commitment to excellence has earned us recognition as one of the UK&#39;s Best Places to Work in games for eight consecutive years by gamesindustry.biz, and we&#39;re proud to be part of the Zynga and Take-Two Interactive family.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Server &amp;amp; Infrastructure Engineer &lt;/strong&gt;to join our server engineering team. In this role, you will work on core backend systems and backend services, contributing directly to live services and build systems with minimal supervision. You will help manage and expand our infrastructure, automated CI/CD pipelines, and development tools while collaborating closely with technical leads to build reliable, high-performing server environments. You will have a passion for large-scale high-availability systems, a devotion to software craftsmanship, an unwavering commitment to quality, and the desire to have their work seen by tens of millions of people worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We embrace a hybrid work environment. Within this role, you would work 2 days per week in our London office and the remaining days at home.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Server &amp;amp; Infrastructure Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Complete multi-day backend engineering tasks with minimal guidance. Design, deploy, and support scalable server architectures and cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DevOps &amp;amp; Pipeline Automation:&lt;/strong&gt; Build, maintain, and optimise robust CI/CD workflows and automated deployment pipelines across cloud environments and build platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture &amp;amp; Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in technical planning, architectural brainstorming, and technical cost/complexity estimation for multi-week efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Efficiency &amp;amp; Quality:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively identify workflow bottlenecks and drive initiatives to improve overall engineering team productivity, tooling, and code quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Participate in internal tech talks, share best practices, and maintain collaborative peer relationships across engineering squads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;Python, Go and C#&lt;/strong&gt; for backend services, automation scripts, and custom tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud Infrastructure &amp;amp; IaC:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience provisioning and managing &lt;strong&gt;AWS&lt;/strong&gt; infrastructure using &lt;strong&gt;Terraform&lt;/strong&gt; (Infrastructure as Code).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build &amp;amp; Platform Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience configuring and managing automated orchestration/build platforms (e.g., &lt;strong&gt;Unreal Horde&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Jenkins&lt;/strong&gt;, or &lt;strong&gt;TeamCity&lt;/strong&gt;), preferably with &lt;strong&gt;Game Engines (Unreal Engine, Unity, etc.)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Source Control Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong working knowledge of version control systems and workflow strategies (&lt;strong&gt;GitHub&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Perforce/Helix Core&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Git-flow&lt;/strong&gt;, branch management).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to manage moderate-to-complex technical tasks independently, break down project deliverables, and communicate status accurately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing server-side logic and managing database dependencies for live applications or multiplayer services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked in, or has a strong interest in the gaming industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in infrastructure deployment and monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in mentoring junior team members or interns, framing task deconstruction, and conducting technical interviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with containerisation (&lt;strong&gt;Docker, Kubernetes&lt;/strong&gt;) and infrastructure security best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer You:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary and discretionary annual bonus scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;26 days holiday, plus bank holidays &amp;amp; 2 paid personal days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 months fully paid maternity/adoption leave and 16 weeks fully paid paternity leave (eligibility criteria applies)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan, with a double matching employer contribution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private medical &amp;amp; dental insurance and healthcare cash plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life insurance, personal accident insurance and income protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and neurodiversity support programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company Employee Stock Purchase Plan (eligibility criteria applies)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fitness reimbursement plan, worth £600 per annum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weekly happy hours, seasonal parties and monthly social events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual rail season ticket advance and cycle to work scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer, which means we are committed to creating and celebrating diverse thoughts, cultures, and backgrounds throughout our organization.&amp;nbsp; Employment with us is based on substantive ability, objective qualifications, and work ethic – not an individual’s race, creed, color, religion, sex or gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin or ancestry, alienage or citizenship status, physical or mental disability, pregnancy, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, status as a victim of domestic violence or sex offenses, reproductive health decision, or any other characteristics protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an equal opportunity employer, we are committed to providing the necessary support and accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities, health conditions, or impairments (subject to any local qualifying requirements) to ensure their full participation in the job application or interview process. Please contact us at ----- to request any accommodations or for support related to your application for an open position.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please be aware that Zynga does not conduct job interviews or make job offers over third-party messaging apps such as Telegram, WhatsApp, or others.&amp;nbsp; Zynga also does not engage in any financial exchanges during the recruitment or onboarding process, and will never ask a candidate for their personal or financial information over an app or other unofficial chat channel.&amp;nbsp; Any attempt to do so may be the result of a scamp or phishing attack, and you should not engage.&amp;nbsp; Zynga’s&amp;nbsp; in-house recruitment team will only contact individuals through their official Company email addresses (i.e., via a zynga.com, take2games.com, naturalmotion.com, smallgiantgames.com, themavens.com, gram.gs email domain).&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Hudl, we build great teams. We hire the best of the best to ensure you’re working with people you can constantly learn from. You’re trusted to get your work done your way while testing the limits of what’s possible and what’s next. We work hard to provide a culture where everyone feels supported, and our employees feel it—their votes helped us become one of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/blog/hudl-2026-top-100-inspiring-workplaces?utm_medium=internal&amp;amp;utm_source=job-ad&amp;amp;utm_campaign=26_NA_talent_job-ad&amp;amp;utm_content=1org_learn-more_blog-link_learn-more_2blog_organic_3ctw&quot;&gt;Top 100 Inspiring Workplaces&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We think of ourselves as the team behind the team, supporting the lifelong impact sports can have: the lessons in teamwork and dedication; the influence of inspiring coaches; and the opportunities to reach new heights. That’s why we help teams from all over the world see their game differently. Our products make it easier for coaches and athletes at any level to capture video, analyze data, share highlights and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ready to join us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1095624224?h=9e8cdc9dbe&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Software Engineer to join our Core Data team in London.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team builds the systems that power how Hudl understands sport at scale. From identifying players and teams across thousands of leagues to processing the moments that become highlights, stats and analysis, our services sit at the centre of Hudl’s platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work on the Global Sports Library (GSL), the backbone that connects identities, metadata and game context across Hudl products. That means designing APIs, distributed services and large-scale data pipelines that help ensure every product at Hudl is operating from the same understanding of the game.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The work is backend-heavy and deeply technical: data modeling, entity resolution, ingestion pipelines, consistency challenges, scalability and platform design. The systems you build won’t just support one product or one sport, they’ll become shared capabilities used across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate across disciplines.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll work closely with a cross-functional team of engineers, quality analysts, product managers and designers to build foundational data tools for the best of the best in sports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver backend-heavy features.&lt;/strong&gt; Your team has the autonomy to build and maintain the GSL, ensuring market teams have access to reliable, comprehensive data infrastructure. We iterate rapidly and deploy changes to our products hundreds of times a day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Propose new solutions.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll have the opportunity to solve complex technical challenges within the Core Data domain and provide guidance to less experienced engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thrive on the front lines.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll build pipelines and libraries that power every feature delivered to coaches and athletes, getting firsthand experience with how our data impacts the game.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time spent collaborating with your teammates in-office will be a regular part of how you work. We&#39;re currently considering applicants within commuting distance of London. You&#39;ll be expected to work more days in-office than remote, but will have the freedom to coordinate your specific in-office schedule with your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong technical proficiency.&lt;/strong&gt; You have at least three years of experience in engineering, specifically within backend-heavy or data-heavy environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve spent time working with cloud-based systems and services and are a strong advocate for TDD and CI/CD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience navigating uncertainty.&lt;/strong&gt; You’re comfortable taking on ambiguous work with many possible implementation options and identifying the one that pragmatically balances quality and immediate customer value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A collaborative, team-first mindset.&lt;/strong&gt; You understand that building great software is a team effort and you’re always willing to pitch in or provide quality feedback in code reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curiosity.&lt;/strong&gt; You enjoy picking up new technologies and domains on the job. The idea of working across foundational layers of our stack and multiple products energizes you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech stack knowledge.&lt;/strong&gt; Professional background in C#, GraphQL, Elastic, MongoDB and AWS is ideal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data infrastructure background.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience working in environments with significant data scale and complex infrastructure needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Familiarity with hybrid teams.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve worked with hybrid or remote teams before and can adapt quickly to our international working environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion work-life harmony&lt;/strong&gt;. We’ll give you the flexibility you need in your work life (e.g., flexible vacation time above any required statutory leave, company-wide holidays and timeout (meeting-free) days, remote work options and more) so you can enjoy your personal life too.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guarantee autonomy&lt;/strong&gt;. We have an open, honest culture and we trust our people from day one. Your team will support you, but you’ll own your work and have the agency to try new ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Encourage career growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;We’re lifelong learners who encourage professional development. We’ll give you tons of resources and opportunities to keep growing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide an environment to help you succeed&lt;/strong&gt;. We&#39;ve invested in our offices, designing incredible spaces with our employees in mind. But whether you’re at the office or working remotely, we’ll provide you the tech you need to do your best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support your wellbeing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Depending on location, we offer medical and retirement benefits for employees—but no matter where you’re located, we have resources like our Employee Assistance Program and employee resource groups to support your mental health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is displayed below—&lt;strong&gt;starting salaries will typically fall near the middle of this range.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make compensation decisions based on an individual&#39;s experience, skills and education in line with our internal pay equity practices.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;£51,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£86,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/jobs/hudl-applicant-and-candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Hudl Applicant and Candidate Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;About THG Ingenuity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;THG Ingenuity is a proprietary Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) technology, robotics, and operations platform built for global ecommerce. Developed through more than two decades of operating ecommerce and retail services at scale, its software and automation capabilities have been engineered, tested, and refined through the real-world demands of managing complex commerce operations. Today, THG Ingenuity provides an integrating operating environment that enables brands to intelligently optimise the entire commerce lifecycle from browsing and checkout to AI inventory management and forecasting, automated fulfilment, carrier control, and customer experience. The platform comprises:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;1&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;THG Fulfil: The fulfilment operating system for global ecommerce. Delivered via a proprietary SaaS and Robotics-as-a-Service (RaaS) model, THG Fulfil orchestrates every stage of checkout, fulfilment, delivery, and customer experience through an integrated system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;1&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;2&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;THG Studios: The UK&#39;s most innovative creative hub, helping brands create content that connects, experiences that engage, and IP that scales, all from its end-to-end, in-house facilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;1&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;hybridMultilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;3&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;THG Commerce: A cloud-native technology stack enabling retailers and brands to create intelligent, AI-powered, digital shopping experiences, while integrated marketplace and social commerce functionality allows brands to reach customers across every sales channel&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;With its expertise in building and scaling brands, THG Ingenuity is uniquely positioned to bring pertinent, pragmatic, and global know-how across all aspects of commerce.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:6,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:6}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About THG Fulfil&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;THG Fulfil is part of THG Ingenuity, providing integrated warehousing, fulfilment and courier management solutions for leading e-commerce brands and enterprise businesses worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Combining advanced warehouse automation with proprietary technology, we help brands scale their operations, improve efficiency and deliver exceptional customer experiences. Our capabilities include AutoStore, Libiao and Geek+ robotics, supported by our own WMS/WCS/OMS platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Solutions Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, you will design innovative, scalable and commercially viable warehouse and fulfilment solutions for THG Fulfil’s enterprise clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with customers, commercial teams, operations, engineering and technology specialists, you will translate complex operational requirements into practical warehouse designs that optimise capacity, throughput, productivity and cost efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will develop end-to-end solutions incorporating warehouse layouts, material flows, storage strategies, automation technologies and systems integration. The role will support both third-party automation opportunities and wider 3PL proposals, including the transition of enterprise customers into THG Fulfil facilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Warehouse Solution Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design end-to-end warehouse and fulfilment solutions for complex enterprise customers, from initial concept through to detailed proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop warehouse layouts, storage strategies, material flows, picking methodologies and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and incorporate automation technologies, including AutoStore, Libiao and Geek+ robotics, based on customer requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess capacity, throughput, labour requirements and operational constraints to ensure solutions are scalable and deliverable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Engagement &amp;amp; Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with enterprise customers to understand operational requirements, order profiles, volumes, growth plans and service-level expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead site visits, operational assessments and discovery workshops to gather requirements and identify opportunities for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer needs into clear technical specifications and tailored fulfilment solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modelling &amp;amp; Commercial Analysis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop capacity plans, throughput models and operational resource requirements using customer data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support solution simulations, cost modelling and ROI analysis to demonstrate the benefits of proposed solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with commercial teams to ensure designs are technically feasible, cost-effective and commercially viable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proposals &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce technical solution proposals incorporating warehouse layouts, process flows, automation configurations and supporting financial analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present solutions to customer stakeholders and support tenders, RFPs and complex sales processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with operations, engineering, software and implementation teams to validate designs and ensure successful delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define integration requirements across THG Fulfil’s WMS/WCS/OMS platforms and automated warehouse equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Experience Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in warehouse solutions design, logistics engineering, intralogistics, automation engineering or supply chain solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing warehouse or fulfilment solutions for large-scale or complex operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of warehouse processes, including storage, replenishment, picking, packing, sortation and dispatch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of warehouse automation, including robotics, automated storage and retrieval systems, conveyors or goods-to-person solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with warehouse layouts, capacity planning, throughput modelling and operational analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial awareness, including experience supporting cost models, ROI calculations and customer proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of WMS, WCS and OMS platforms and their integration with warehouse automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving and communication skills, with the ability to present complex solutions clearly to technical and commercial stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Experience within 3PL, contract logistics or e-commerce fulfilment, with exposure to AutoStore, Libiao, Geek+ or warehouse design and simulation tools.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THG Ingenuity is proud to be a Disability Confident Committed employer. If you are invited to interview, please let us know if there are any reasonable adjustments we can make to the recruitment process that will enable you to perform to the best of your ability.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THG Ingenuity is committed to creating a diverse &amp;amp; inclusive environment and hence welcomes applications from all sections of the community.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Because of the high volumes of applications our opportunities attract, it sometimes takes us time to review and consider them all. We endeavour to respond to every application we receive within 14 days. If you haven&#39;t heard from us within that time frame or should you have any specific questions about this or other applications for positions at THG Ingenuity please contact one of our &lt;span class=&quot;mark75xs2u5gf&quot; data-markjs=&quot;true&quot; data-ogac=&quot;&quot; data-ogab=&quot;&quot; data-ogsc=&quot;&quot; data-ogsb=&quot;&quot;&gt;Talent&lt;/span&gt; team to discuss further.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

